WEBVTT

00:02:58.954 --> 00:03:01.871
despite having buildings
full of computers.

00:03:03.121 --> 00:03:05.746
We had to start distributing
the petabytes of data

00:03:05.788 --> 00:03:07.204
to our collaborating partners

00:03:07.246 --> 00:03:09.454
in order to employ 
local computing and storage

00:03:09.496 --> 00:03:12.163
at hundreds of different institutes.

00:03:12.413 --> 00:03:14.954
In order to orchestrate
these interconnected resources

00:03:14.996 --> 00:03:18.538
with their diverse technologies,
we developed a computing grid,

00:03:18.579 --> 00:03:23.371
enabling the seamless sharing
of computing resources around the globe.

00:03:23.413 --> 00:03:26.913
This relies on trust relationships
and mutual exchange.

00:03:27.121 --> 00:03:29.246
But this grid model
could not be transferred

00:03:29.288 --> 00:03:31.288
out of our community so easily,